WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.801
We are following a developing

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.169
story out of Nairobi in Kenya

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.271
about a gas explosion

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.273
that's left at least three people dead

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:10.577
and 280 others wounded.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.318
According to the Kenyan government,

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:21.121
a huge ball of fire was caused by gas

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.422
that a truck was carrying.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:25.158
It apparently exploded at a gas plant

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.860
For more on the story

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.229
and a look at the scene of destruction,

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.263
we are joined by Larry.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.833
Hi, Larry. Hi, Max.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:34.567
We don't know

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.236
the cause of this explosion,

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:39.072
but we know that this should not be here.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.740
This is a liquefied

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.676
petroleum gas store and filling plant.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.279
Cooking gas is a very common,

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:47.614
commonly used across

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.416
not just Kenya, but across East Africa.

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.850
But this place was unlicensed

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.085
and therefore illegal

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:53.086
The regulator here in

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.721
Kenya says they applied for licenses

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.990
in March, in June and in July,

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.725
and they were denied all three times

00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.726
for safety reasons

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.461
that to close to residential area

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.630
and therefore, in the event of a blast

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.931
like what happened last night,

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.032
it would affect so many people

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.000
that live around here

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.835
because this is a densely populated area.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.870
And in fact, that is what happened.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:12.572
So the question

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.207
for so many in this community is

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.342
why was this allowed to be here so long

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.644
even after the place was demolished

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:18.778
at least twice,

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.013
according to the Petroleum

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.181
Institute of East Africa,

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.916
and the owner of this place

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:25.952
was even convicted and jailed.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.353
Should have gone to jail for five years,

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.588
only to have the one year sentence

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:29.422
and then came right back

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.123
to doing it again.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.192
And this is the impact of that

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.098
a huge ball of fire

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:40.100
ignited over Nairobi's night sky

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.768
only heard

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.070
the screams of onlookers

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.340
piercing through the sound of flames.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:50.143
Emergency workers racing to the scene

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:52.145
after a gas truck exploded

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.546
at what officials are calling

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.148
an unlicensed plant late

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.282
Thursday evening,

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.784
burning down a warehouse

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.720
and damaging surrounding homes.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:03.223
The tears of this woman

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:05.492
falling on to a lost loved one.

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.759
Multiple dead

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:09.229
with hundreds of others wounded.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.264
So as I'm about to come one kilometer,

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:12.866
we would only talk.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:13.466
I knew

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.602
why the fire caught up with me

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.036
from almost one kilometer away

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.571
as I was escaping.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:19.772
The flames from the explosion

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:20.473
knocked me down

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.875
burnt me on my neck and back,

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:23.276
as you can see.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.111
Nairobi police are calling it

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:26.079
a crime scene

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.314
and opened an investigation on Friday.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:29.883
Nearby, residents

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:32.118
watching in silent shock

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:32.619
as crime

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.587
investigators dig through the ash

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.289
at less than 24 hours ago

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.090
where their homes

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.660
business has hollowed out

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:41.794
this cause of the flames

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.997
abandoned these shop walls.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.298
The extent of the damage

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:47.967
spreading for miles.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:50.436
The gas explosion brings down everything

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:50.970
in its wake,

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:51.971
distracts

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.439
several structures, several hundred

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.974
yards in every direction.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.342
One of the sixth floor rooftop,

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.977
almost one of the yards away,

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.312
broke down this wall

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.747
and most dramatic of all.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:03.616
A car that was blasted all this way.

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.019
Parts of the car here, the rest of it

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.021
strewn all across this area.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.589
And we're just a mile away

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:10.790
from Kenya's main airport

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.193
as we see a plane landing there.

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:15.862
Residents

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:16.896
of that building

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:19.232
telling me of their frantic escape

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:21.734
We don't and they fly on top of us.

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:25.171
So the gate was closed,

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.974
but we there was a stampede.

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:29.809
We hurriedly tried to get out.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:30.643
I think

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.246
very many people were actually injured

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:33.980
at that moment.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:37.517
Government officials

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:38.885
already dubbing the incident

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.920
as a consequence of corruption,

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.322
vowing to shut down

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:44.023
the unlicensed company

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.925
who was operating inside the cooking

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.760
gas filling plant.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.530
It is totally immoral for one to risk

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:52.565
lives of fellow Kenyans

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.934
just for profit, mere profiteering.

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:58.705
It is not acceptable for such facilities.

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:00.073
To be resident

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.908
within residential areas

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.676
because these are innocent hustlers

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.311
who are going through their businesses

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.679
on a daily basis.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.482
Rebuilding the damage could take months

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.184
or even years.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:11.918
But in the hours

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:13.052
ahead, families

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.221
now having to face the reality of grief

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:18.291
right now.

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:19.292
So back on the street,

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.461
look at the damage in this car.

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:22.495
There's so many of them

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.097
across this neighborhood.

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:26.165
And this is just the impact of that

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:28.534
gas explosion that you see in this area.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:29.035
The building

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:29.636
you saw in that piece,

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:31.471
by the way, that all the way back there,

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:33.573
you see the damage on the wall.

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.041
And the most extraordinary thing

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.576
having been in this scene,

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:38.678
because it's a densely populated area.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.113
This explosion,

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:42.215
if it happened in the middle of the day,

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.683
there could have been hundreds

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:44.550
of casualties.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.452
All the people you see here around.

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.854
These are people that live here.

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:48.988
If they were out on the streets

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:49.956
going about their business

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.391
and this happened.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:52.592
The devastation would

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.493
have been unspeakable things.

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:56.562
Yeah, it's one blessing, isn't it?

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:57.664
Larry, thank you so much for

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:58.798
joining us from Nairobi.

